# A created deck's and a created Word document's captured parts are stored and written exactly as the
# reference produced them, and their line endings differ part by part, so each must keep its own bytes
# (the crate's `writing/pptx/create/parts.rs` and `writing/docx/create/parts.rs` record the measured
# mix). Each rule is scoped to its own directory alone — a blanket setting would also rewrite
# `assets/docgen/document-kit.js`, whose digest is part of the reference writer's identity.
/document-engine/assets/pptx-create/** -text
/document-engine/assets/docx-create/** -text

# The oracle's kept PDFs are the outside reference's own output, stored and written exactly as it
# produced them: a line-ending conversion would change the digest that says a second run reproduces
# the file, and the pages a reviewer reads.
/oracle/record/documents/**/produced.pdf -text

# The oracle's font configuration is compared byte for byte against the one this machine's font set
# makes, so a line-ending conversion would break the comparison.
/oracle/record/fonts.conf -text
